  "title": "Kourovka problem 18.114 (main)",
  "statement": {
    "representation": "pdf-text-entry",
    "text": "Does there exist an irreducible 5′ -subgroup G of GL(V ) for some finite F5 -\nspace V such that the number of conjugacy classes of the semidirect product V G is\nequal to |V | but G is not cyclic?\n   Such a subgroup exists if 5 is replaced by p = 2, 3 but does not exist for primes\np > 5 (J. Group Theory, 14 (2011), 175–199).                               P. Schmid",
